{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "no-receipt-limits",
  "title": "No-receipt return limits",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "658c3eff-e609-404a-8299-16a9b5babdf4",
      "question": "What does the loss-prevention memo set as the maximum value of a no-receipt return, how many no-receipt returns can one customer make in 90 days, and what is the lower limit at stores on enhanced monitoring?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-03T04:15:45.062251Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-03T04:15:50.991415Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "Based on the Asset Protection loss-prevention memo (AP-2026-031, effective August 15, 2026):\n\n| Rule | Value |\n|------|-------|\n| Maximum value of a no-receipt return (standard) | **$75.00 per transaction**, refunded as store credit only [1] |\n| Maximum no-receipt returns per customer in 90 days | **3 no-receipt returns** in any rolling 90-day period [1] |\n| Lowered no-receipt limit at enhanced-monitoring stores | **$50.00 per transaction** (applies to stores S06 Newark Gateway, S22 Los Angeles Westside, S16 Indianapolis Fashion Mall from Aug 15 – Dec 31, 2026) [1] |\n\nThe memo also requires the cashier to scan the customer’s photo ID for every no-receipt return.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Unstructured Retrieval evidence — 3 documents — evidence `hermes-receipt:4e0f7247b758c35e68c352f0f41cec4d2b7e159d7feec6c03458bcdec29361d0`",
